      | A list is stored only if its records are            | a list of records that name no table is refused when the model is built, naming the field                     | stored-records: A model the types cannot describe is refused                   |                                                                                                                                                                        |
      | One record without a table lives in its owner's row | a record with no table held as one field is stored in its owner's row, as <field>_<subfield> columns          | value-records: Ddl prints a value's columns and the CHECK for an optional one  | Apply the comment's naming rule, the field's name and then the subfield's, to the City of a Depot's Place.                                                             |
